/private/var/folders/80/jm5p82hn56g0crpvv9xjzrc00000gn/T/jc2-lane.EfPwqb/inputs/d1-subtree-review-grok46-20260902.md:147:`M_1=-m<M_2<...<M_s=n-2` (Moh search (1),(2); Def 5.1), and Lemma 5.2 gives `delta_r<1`, `n-M_r>0`. The gap vanishes iff `M_r=-m` iff `r=1`, and is strictly negative for `r>=2`. Verified on 8000 census V-skeletons (`n<=120`) and on all six Moh rows: equality at `r=1`, never at `r>=2`.
