     5	The full multiset of ultrametric distances is read off Newton polygons:
     6	    Res_y( g(x,y), h(x, y+w) )  has w-roots exactly { h-root_j - g-root_i },
     7	so its Newton polygon in w gives the multiset { ord_t(rho_i - phi_j) }.
     8	With h = g this gives the g-g contacts (plus a w^n factor from i=j).
     9	
    10	For a ONE-PLACE g (nu = 1) every g-root is Galois-conjugate to every other, so
    11	the per-root contact profile is the aggregate divided by n, and the tree is
    12	determined.  D1-STAR is then checkable directly.
