   229	### 2.5 The bottom partition theorem
   230	
   231	**[PROVED-HERE/UNREVIEWED]** Substitute \(M_1=-m\) in the terminal equation:
   232	
   233	\[
   234	 nP_1Q_1'-mQ_1P_1'=c,\qquad c\ne0. \tag{BOT}
   235	\]
   236	
   237	If \(\alpha\) were a repeated root of \(P_1\), then
   238	\(P_1(\alpha)=P_1'(\alpha)=0\), so the left side of `(BOT)` would vanish at
   239	\(\alpha\), contradicting \(c\ne0\). The identical argument applies to a
   240	repeated root of \(Q_1\). A common root of \(P_1,Q_1\) also makes the left side
   241	zero. Hence \(P_1Q_1\) is squarefree.
   242	
   243	The degree rescaling makes Moh's Appendix-I statement apply verbatim:
   244	
   245	\[
   246	 (n,m)=\frac{K}{V_2}(A,B),\qquad
