I’m adding a direct resultant check for the `A_bot` witness now, separate from the tree-contact computation. The tree tells us there are five D1 discs of size 3; the resultant degree is the independent `N=1` check.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
import sympy as sp
x,y=sp.symbols('x y')
c1=sp.Rational(7,3); c2=sp.Rational(-5,2)
f=x+y**5
g=y+(x+y**5)**3
R=sp.expand(sp.resultant(sp.Poly(f-c1,y), sp.Poly(g-c2,y), y).as_expr())
J=sp.expand(sp.diff(f,x)*sp.diff(g,y)-sp.diff(f,y)*sp.diff(g,x))
print('J=',J)
print('deg_y f,g=',sp.degree(f,y),sp.degree(g,y))
print('resultant=',sp.factor(R))
print('deg_x resultant=',sp.degree(R,x))
print('leading coeff in x=',sp.LC(sp.Poly(R,x)))
PY" in /Users/dc/code/math/jc2
